 1. G-L7 rule (e) — A GATE MAY NOT RE-DERIVE ITS OWN ORACLE. Clause (2c)
    compared the rendered `.wave-char` span count against `glyphCount`, which
    was computed at `:239` from `mirrorText` — the subject's OWN rendering of
    the title. The equality therefore held BY CONSTRUCTION, and a formally
    discharged defect survived a HARD-in-CI browser gate (KF-AT-4). The oracle
    now comes from OUTSIDE the subject: `DECLARED_HERO_TITLE`, read statically
    from `EditorStartScreen.vue`'s own `title:` prop default (the clause-1
    idiom this file already uses for scenes.ts / router.ts). The mirror count
    is still REPORTED (`mirrorGlyphCount`) so a divergence is legible, and
    clause (2b) gains a new bite: the mirror must spell the DECLARED title.
    A missing declaration THROWS rather than falling back to the mirror.

 2. KF-AT-24 / R-3's FOLD — the private AnimatedText class strings had three
    homes (this file's `:20-31` contract + `:188`/`:218` live queries,
    `font-roles.json`'s pin, and the component). They now have ONE:
    `demo/styles/font-roles.json`'s `hero-display` row, exported as
    `SELECTORS` by `scripts/gates/register-census.mjs`. This gate and the
    register census read the same contract, so a rename to `kf-split` REDs
    BOTH instead of silently voiding both. Every query (`heroReady`'s poll at
    `:160-172`, the word/char tiers, (2d)'s ink probe) is re-pointed; the two
    remaining `.wave-word` mentions are PROSE in comments and select nothing.

DEPENDENCY, stated: this half requires `scripts/gates/register-census.mjs` and
the `wordWrapperSelector` field on `font-roles.json`'s `hero-display` row —
